# This project breaks each baseline spec rule at least one time.
# The expected output records the message and the fix text of each rule.
exits 1 sv check
cmp stdout check.txt
! stderr .

# A spec with only warnings passes, unless you set --strict.
exits 0 sv check specs/warn.yaml
cmp stdout warn.txt
exits 1 sv check --strict specs/warn.yaml
cmp stdout warn.txt

exits 1 sv check --format json specs/rules.yaml
cmp stdout rules.json

-- .specval.yaml --
specs_dir: specs
-- .specval/data/services.yaml --
services:
  OrderManager: { layer: manager }
  PricingEngine: { layer: engine }
  OrderAccessor: { layer: accessor }
  BillingAccessor: { layer: accessor }
-- specs/pass.yaml --
specval: 1
id: PASS-1
kind: feature
title: A spec that passes
summary: OrderManager reads an order.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: "Given an order, when it is read, then it is returned." }
services:
  changed: [OrderManager]
calls:
  - { from: OrderManager, to: OrderAccessor, op: GetOrder, covers: [AC1] }
-- specs/warn.yaml --
specval: 1
id: WARN-1
kind: chore
title: A spec with only a warning
summary: BillingAccessor is listed as changed, but no call uses it.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: "Given an order, when it is read, then it is returned." }
services:
  changed: [BillingAccessor]
calls:
  - { from: OrderManager, to: OrderAccessor, op: GetOrder, covers: [AC1] }
-- specs/rules.yaml --
specval: 1
id: RULES-1
kind: feature
title: A spec that breaks each spec rule
summary: Each part of this spec breaks one rule.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: Covered. }
  - { id: AC2, text: Not covered by a call. }
services:
  new:
    - { name: RefundCalc, layer: engine, purpose: Has no layer suffix. }
    - { name: TaxManager, layer: engine, purpose: Has the suffix of a different layer. }
    - { name: PricingEngine, layer: engine, purpose: Is already registered. }
    - { name: AuditHelper, layer: helper, purpose: Has an unknown layer. }
    - { name: UnusedEngine, layer: engine, purpose: Is not in a call. }
    - { name: CacheResource, layer: resource, purpose: Calls a service. }
  changed: [GhostManager, BillingAccessor]
calls:
  - { from: OrderManager, to: RefundCalc, op: Calculate, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: OrderManager, to: TaxManager, op: Tax, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: PricingEngine, to: OrderManager, op: Notify, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: OrderAccessor, to: PricingEngine, op: Reprice, covers: [AC9] }
  - { from: CacheResource, to: OrderAccessor, op: Fill, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: OrderManager, to: MysteryEngine, op: Run, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: Somebody, to: OrderAccessor, op: Run, covers: [AC1] }
-- specs/yaml.yaml --
specval: 1
id: [unclosed
-- specs/empty.yaml --
-- specs/shape.yaml --
specval: 2
id: bad id
kind: feature
title: ""
summary: Wrong shapes.
acceptance:
  - { id: A1, text: Bad id. }
services:
  new:
    - { name: lowerEngine, layer: engine }
  removed: []
calls:
  - { from: OrderManager, to: OrderAccessor, op: get-order }
owner: someone
-- check.txt --
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 acceptance is required
    fix: Add `acceptance`: The acceptance criteria. Give one or more, and make each one possible to test.
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 calls is required
    fix: Add `calls`: Each call from one service to another that this change adds or changes.
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 id is required
    fix: Add `id`: The ID of the ticket, for example ORD-142. Use letters, digits, '.', '_', and '-'. Name the spec file <id>.yaml.
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 kind is required
    fix: Add `kind`: The kind of change: feature, bugfix, or chore.
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 specval is required
    fix: Add `specval`: The version of the spec format. It is always 1.
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 summary is required
    fix: Add `summary`: A short paragraph that tells the problem and the new behavior.
specs/empty.yaml:1 error SV001 title is required
    fix: Add `title`: The title of the change, on one line.
specs/rules.yaml:8 error SV107 No call covers AC2 (acceptance[1])
    fix: Add AC2 to `covers` on the call(s) that implement it, or add the missing call.
specs/rules.yaml:11 error SV103 RefundCalc is in the engine layer but does not end in Engine (services.new[0].name)
    fix: Change its name to RefundCalcEngine everywhere in the spec, or change its layer.
specs/rules.yaml:12 error SV103 TaxManager is in the engine layer but does not end in Engine (services.new[1].name)
    fix: Change its name to TaxEngine everywhere in the spec, or change its layer.
specs/rules.yaml:13 error SV104 PricingEngine is already registered (engine layer) (services.new[2].name)
    fix: Move PricingEngine from services.new to services.changed.
specs/rules.yaml:14 error SV105 helper is not a layer (services.new[3].layer)
    fix: Use one of: manager, engine, accessor, resource.
specs/rules.yaml:14 error SV106 AuditHelper is in services.new, but no call uses it (services.new[3])
    fix: Add the calls to or from AuditHelper, or remove it from services.new.
specs/rules.yaml:15 error SV106 UnusedEngine is in services.new, but no call uses it (services.new[4])
    fix: Add the calls to or from UnusedEngine, or remove it from services.new.
specs/rules.yaml:17 error SV109 GhostManager is not a registered service (services.changed[0])
    fix: If GhostManager is new, move it to services.new with a layer and purpose. Otherwise use a registered service: OrderManager.
specs/rules.yaml:17 warning SV201 BillingAccessor is in services.changed, but no call uses it (services.changed[1])
    fix: Add the calls that change BillingAccessor, or remove it from services.changed.
specs/rules.yaml:21 error SV102 PricingEngine (engine) cannot call OrderManager (manager) (calls[2])
    fix: Engines can call only accessors. No service can call managers.
specs/rules.yaml:22 error SV102 OrderAccessor (accessor) cannot call PricingEngine (engine) (calls[3])
    fix: Accessors can call only resources. Send the call to PricingEngine through a manager.
specs/rules.yaml:22 error SV108 AC9 is not an acceptance criterion in this spec (calls[3].covers[0])
    fix: Use one of: AC1, AC2, or add AC9 under acceptance.
specs/rules.yaml:23 error SV102 CacheResource (resource) cannot call OrderAccessor (accessor) (calls[4])
    fix: Resources cannot call other services. Send the call to OrderAccessor through a manager or engine.
specs/rules.yaml:24 error SV101 MysteryEngine is not a registered service (calls[5].to)
    fix: If MysteryEngine is new, declare it under services.new with a layer and purpose. Otherwise use a registered service: PricingEngine.
specs/rules.yaml:25 error SV101 Somebody is not a registered service (calls[6].from)
    fix: If Somebody is new, declare it under services.new with a layer and purpose. Otherwise use a registered service: BillingAccessor, OrderAccessor, OrderManager, PricingEngine.
specs/shape.yaml:1 error SV001 specval does not match: 1 (specval)
    fix: Correct the value of `specval`. The version of the spec format. It is always 1.
specs/shape.yaml:1 error SV001 Additional property owner is not allowed
    fix: Remove `owner`, or correct its name. The permitted fields here are: acceptance, calls, id, kind, out_of_scope, services, specval, status, summary, title.
specs/shape.yaml:2 error SV001 Does not match pattern '^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$' (id)
    fix: Correct the value of `id`. The ID of the ticket, for example ORD-142. Use letters, digits, '.', '_', and '-'. Name the spec file <id>.yaml.
specs/shape.yaml:4 error SV001 String length must be greater than or equal to 1 (title)
    fix: Correct the value of `title`. The title of the change, on one line.
specs/shape.yaml:7 error SV001 Does not match pattern '^AC[0-9]+$' (acceptance[0].id)
    fix: Correct the value of `acceptance[0].id`. AC and a number, for example AC1.
specs/shape.yaml:8 error SV001 Additional property removed is not allowed (services)
    fix: Remove `removed`, or correct its name. The permitted fields here are: changed, new.
specs/shape.yaml:10 error SV001 purpose is required (services.new[0])
    fix: Add `purpose`: One sentence that tells what the service does.
specs/shape.yaml:10 error SV001 Does not match pattern '^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*$' (services.new[0].name)
    fix: Correct the value of `services.new[0].name`. A PascalCase name that ends with the suffix of its layer, for example RefundEngine.
specs/shape.yaml:13 error SV001 covers is required (calls[0])
    fix: Add `covers`: The acceptance criteria that this call helps to satisfy, for example [AC1].
specs/shape.yaml:13 error SV001 Does not match pattern '^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*$' (calls[0].op)
    fix: Correct the value of `calls[0].op`. The name of the operation, in PascalCase, for example CalculateRefund.
specs/warn.yaml:9 warning SV201 BillingAccessor is in services.changed, but no call uses it (services.changed[0])
    fix: Add the calls that change BillingAccessor, or remove it from services.changed.
specs/yaml.yaml:1 error SV000 yaml: line 1: did not find expected ',' or ']'
    fix: Fix the YAML syntax at this line.
specval checked 6 spec(s) and found 32 error(s) and 2 warning(s).
-- warn.txt --
specs/warn.yaml:9 warning SV201 BillingAccessor is in services.changed, but no call uses it (services.changed[0])
    fix: Add the calls that change BillingAccessor, or remove it from services.changed.
specval checked 1 spec(s) and found 0 error(s) and 1 warning(s).
